Why it is here (docs/source-form.md, group E step 7): the AM62P's D-PHY TX and DSI host
are written from the AM62Px TRM (TI SPRUJ83D) in driver/rust/src/ip/cdns_{dphy,dsi}.rs.
Where the TRM is silent the source is TI's own driver, vendored unmodified: the D-PHY's
data-rate band table, the PLL gm PWM divider values, the WIZ registers' place in the
D-PHY region, and the MCTL_DPHY_CFG0 sequence. The file is not compiled (it is a whole
Zephyr driver for another binding, ti,j721e-dsi, and another clock API); the generator
reads those four facts out of it. driver/docs/am62p-display-cold.md has the table of
what the TRM documents and what comes from here.

